From e5f68d0bb6126bf4768ef72244b4598f26b55371 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudy Cato <rudy@americanfoodbeverage.local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:23:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Security hardening + database backups
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Security:
- CORS restricted to ALLOWED_ORIGINS env var instead of wildcard
- Session cookie gets Secure flag automatically in production
  (COOKIE_SECURE, defaults true unless running on local SQLite)
- Staff accounts now carry must_change_password; login redirects to
  a forced password-change screen until it's cleared
- New /auth/change-password endpoint, /change-password page (also
  usable voluntarily any time via dashboard header link)

Backups:
- New admin.py router: /admin/backup/local (download JSON snapshot
  of every table), /admin/backup/cloud (push to S3-compatible
  storage if BACKUP_S3_* env vars are set), /admin/backup/history
- New BackupLog model tracks every attempt (who, when, size, status)
- Dashboard: new 'Data & Backups' panel, admin-only, with both
  buttons and a history table
- Cloud backup fails with a clear actionable message (not a 500)
  when storage isn't configured yet
- render.yaml: added optional BACKUP_S3_* env var placeholders
  (sync: false — fill in via Render dashboard when ready)
